+
+### Logging (BBAI and SASGameRecord)
+
 - **BBAI logging is now XML-tunable:** BBAI AI-decision logging can now be enabled/disabled and adjusted through **SAS defines**, rather than editing and recompiling the DLL as in base AdvCiv. This is deemed valuable **not only for modders, but also for users** who can now view or generate `BBAI.log` files for review. Note: `LoggingEnabled=1` in `CivilizationIV.ini` is still required for Civ4 to write. This allowed for example to surgically identify and fix the root cause of a city not producing its first settler until ~T90 at normal game speed, which is way too late (`bWarPlan` was too aggressively gating settler production; now it only blocks settler production after early expansion has reached enough cities (inefficient at that point, better switch strategy)). Note: BBAI logs can be very long; for broad raw-log diagnosis, we usually give to an external LLM/AI such as ChatGPT the log file, as it is as of now agentic-token-free analysis (also good to give us a different point of view/review if needed).
 - **Timestamped BBAI log files:** Optionally log each new game and loaded save to a **new UTC-timestamped file** (e.g., `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_new1.log` or `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_load2.log`) instead of expanding the existing `BBAI.log`, which was very tedious to clean up or identify/store/read/review/upload, and so repeated save-file tests no longer require restarting Civ4. Each log begins notably with the new/load time, currently active BBAI log levels, turn/year, map and game settings (including `landheavy` and `navalheavy` actual game information), player counts, and RNG states, avoiding mixed logs and the need to restart Civ4 between repeated save-file tests. See also [README.md (BBAI logging and head example)](/README.md#bbai-logging-and-head-example).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6022+) **SAS game-record log:** added a separate `SASGameRecord_*.log` for compact autoplay and AI-strength review. It notably records high-level run context such as initial map/landmass geography and bonus/yield context, economy, expansion, city and battle history, worked plots, diplomacy, unit composition, game state, and in-game bonus appearances/disappearances, complementing BBAI logs by recording what happened before or alongside detailed AI-decision traces. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6033+) It also logs autoplay start/end/change rows, explicit player appearance/revival/elimination rows, and compact run-status rows with alive/eliminated players, current winner/victory if any, and top score/power players, so stopped autoplay logs no longer require inferring these from missing snapshots. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6034+) Free-text fields such as city, player, leader, civ, map-script, and log-file names are quoted/escaped, so names with spaces are easier to parse robustly. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6057+) It also notably records compact per-turn exploration, map changes and environmental status, explicit spaceship launches and project-victory progress, and a full final snapshot when the game is won.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6058+) It notably also records war-declaration causes and sponsors, diplomacy memories, progress for all enabled victories, project-victory resets and failures, and compact full-map revelation. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6077+) It notably also further records active mod and DLL-slot identity, research and production overflow, production conversion and lost-production gold, city buildings and pollution, trade unlocks, and compact territory development including routes, improvements, irrigation, and improved/unimproved bonus types, and also names player-wide health/happiness modifier sources and records AI victory-stage strategies and the target's victory context when war is declared. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6091+) It also records `UnitCombat` shares alongside raw army-composition counts, compact air/missile/nuclear posture including carrier and missile cargo, and per-city air-unit occupancy/capacity. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6092+) It also records current/undamaged city-defense state and bombard damage on city snapshots, synthetic consecutive city-bombard sequences with actual before/after defense reduction and unit counts, plus individual air strikes, interceptions, and plot-air-bomb attempts so military-unit ownership can be compared with actual tactical use.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6100+) It also records compact production and military interval flows plus exact civic, effective state-religion, and war-plan transitions. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6101+) Technology-acquisition rows also identify whether each technology came from research, trade, a free choice, a goody hut, a Great Person, espionage, a random event, technology sharing, a team merge, inheritance, Advanced Start, Barbarian research, game setup, debug tools, or an unknown Python/script source. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6102+) Each log also identifies whether the session is a new or loaded single-player, scenario, network, Hotseat, PBEM, Pitboss, or replay game, including its multiplayer turn options. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6103+) It also synthesizes one summary for every war between civilization teams, including declaration and peace context, elapsed turns, war-success changes, units destroyed and their total production cost, city-plot battle wins, and cities/population captured. Wars already active when a save is loaded are explicitly partial, while wars still active at victory or autoplay end remain marked ongoing rather than being misreported as peace. A full turn-474 test matched all 115 declarations to exactly 91 ordinary-peace summaries, 4 capitulations, 13 state-change/elimination summaries, and 7 wars still ongoing at victory.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6105+) Setup context also records the calendar, starting turn/year, and each player's actual assigned color with its primary RGB values, which helps connect the text record to maps and screenshots. When the game is won, one final row per civilization pairs its ordinary score with Civ4's normalized final score. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6104+) Full interval and victory snapshots also record UTC to milliseconds, total real milliseconds since the log session began, and milliseconds since the previous snapshot. This makes autoplay speed and late-game slowdown directly comparable without external timing or timestamp subtraction; real time includes pauses and user interaction. Anonymous process-memory, system memory-load percentage, available 32-bit address space, and exact foreground/minimized samples can be disabled separately without disabling timing or gameplay records. A separate privacy/detail level defaults to display context (resolution, fullscreen/windowed state, and graphics options), Windows versus Wine/Proton, and pointer width; it can be lowered to hide these or raised to add logical processor count and total RAM.
-- Note: it currently contains spoilers: a spoiler-free implementation was considered, so the human/active player can give to an LLM or such their play summary and get LLM or such suggestions or feedback/analysis, but it would require an extensive rework, so currently this is not supported; therefore, SAS game-record log should as of now not be treated as a spoiler-free player-advice export. Note 2: depending on `SAS_GAME_RECORD_INTERVAL_TURNS_UNSCALED_GAMESPEED` value, the last turn may not appear in the log: for example, an autoplay run of 200 turns ends at T200 and thus does not seem to show the T200 data, only up to T190, so autoplay at least 201 turns to show T200 for example if you have this issue. For stronger LLM analysis, also provide compact source context when possible; for example, the AdvCiv-SAS light source ZIP from [`make_light_source_zip.py`](/LLM_Helpers/README.md#make_light_source_zippy) includes useful source/XML/docs/helper context while staying compact enough to upload and share. See also [README.md (DLL Logging)](/README.md#dll-logging).
 - **BBAI worker log split:** added separate worker and Work Boat / `UNITAI_WORKER_SEA` BBAI log-level defines so ordinary `SAS_BBAI_UNIT_LOG_LEVEL` can focus on non-worker unit behavior such as scrapping, army movement, and combat-unit decisions. Worker and worker-sea logs had become noisy enough to hide those unit decisions, and Work Boats use distinct logic from land workers, so they now have their own category as well.
 - **BBAI Settler log split:** added `SAS_BBAI_SETTLER_LOG_LEVEL`, separated from UNIT so Settlers and other units can be inspected independently. This notably covers city-site decisions, Settler movement, scouting, returns, founding, (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6027+) parking reasons, danger context, and city escort pools; FOUND as of now separately controls detailed city-site scoring calculations. This notably lets UNIT investigate other unit behavior without enabling the multi-megabyte first-city Settler traces needed for example for the Berlin, Karakorum, and Cuzco regression tests.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6062+) **Overseas-transport BBAI diagnostics:** added `SAS_BBAI_OVERSEAS_TRANSPORT_LOG_LEVEL`, separated from CITY and UNIT so overseas settlement and conquest logistics can be inspected without enabling those broad logs. It notably connects known valuable island sites and cities with their distance and defenders, map type, transport production and cargo capacity, loaded units, units actually available to board, incoming cargo already assigned within 1/3/7 turns, pickup/loading failures, launch thresholds and decisions, naval reachability, and Settler/Worker cargo handling.
